<title>UK: London tea auction saw good general demand.</title>
<headline>London tea auction saw good general demand.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Good general demand was noted at Monday's tea auction at which Assams were firm, with better sorts often dearer, the official report said.</p>
<p>Best Kenyas were sometimes lower but most east Africans were fully firm. The few Ceylons were strong and dearer.</p>
<p>The offshore sector found medium Kenyas and Zimbabwes sold well at firm rates.</p>
<p>The next auction will be held on Monday, November 25.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 8074</p>
</text>
